From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] DVDDemuxFFmpeg: a cover picture is not a Dolby Vision layer

A dual-layer Dolby Vision file carries its base and enhancement layers as
two video tracks, and the demuxer pairs a Dolby Vision track with any
other video track it finds. A cut of a single-layer Dolby Vision film
kept its cover picture as a one-frame MJPEG video track: the film was
taken for the enhancement layer of the cover, and the player, which
never opens an enhancement layer on its own, played the cover instead
of the film.

Both layers of a pair are HEVC or AVC now, and the base layer looked
up for an enhancement layer is one too, so a picture track is left as
the extra track it is and the film plays.

The pairing is CoreELEC's own Dolby Vision code in the shared demuxer,
so the change has to be there.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp
@@ -2241,7 +2241,7 @@
 
         // check if it's dual video stream and one of it is type DV
         auto it = std::find_if(m_streams.begin(), m_streams.end(),
-          [&st, &matchesLegacyPartner](const std::pair<int, CDemuxStream*>& v)
+          [&st, &matchesLegacyPartner, pStream](const std::pair<int, CDemuxStream*>& v)
           {
             if (v.second->type != StreamType::VIDEO)
               return false;
@@ -2249,6 +2249,11 @@
             if (!matchesLegacyPartner(v.first))
               return false;
             CDemuxStreamVideo* vs = static_cast<CDemuxStreamVideo*>(v.second);
+            // both layers are HEVC or AVC: a cover picture is not a base layer
+            const AVCodecID codec = pStream->codecpar->codec_id;
+            if ((vs->codec != AV_CODEC_ID_HEVC && vs->codec != AV_CODEC_ID_H264) ||
+                (codec != AV_CODEC_ID_HEVC && codec != AV_CODEC_ID_H264))
+              return false;
             return (vs->hdr_type == StreamHdrType::HDR_TYPE_DOLBYVISION) ||
                    (st->hdr_type == StreamHdrType::HDR_TYPE_DOLBYVISION);
           });
@@ -2274,7 +2279,9 @@
 
                   if (!matchesLegacyPartner(v.first))
                     return false;
-                  return static_cast<CDemuxStreamVideo*>(v.second)->hdr_type != StreamHdrType::HDR_TYPE_DOLBYVISION;
+                  const auto* vs = static_cast<CDemuxStreamVideo*>(v.second);
+                  return vs->hdr_type != StreamHdrType::HDR_TYPE_DOLBYVISION &&
+                         (vs->codec == AV_CODEC_ID_HEVC || vs->codec == AV_CODEC_ID_H264);
                 });
 
               if (it != m_streams.end())
